.SH NAME
sleep \- suspend execution for an interval
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsleep \fItime\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sleep
suspends execution for
.I time
seconds.
It is used to execute a command
after a 105 seconds, as in:
.PP
	(sleep 105; command)&
.PP
or to execute a command every 37 seconds, as in:
.PP
	while true
.br
	do
.br
		command
.br
		sleep 37
.br
	done
.SH SEE ALSO
wait(1), alarm(2), sleep(3).
.SH LIMITATIONS
.I Time
must be less than 65536 seconds.
